,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T02:41:15-07:00","id":1337458,"title":"","content":"Well, first Samatsu (the fire swordsman) and the Air Aspect from Adversaries of the Righteous, and 150 soldiers, fought the whole party. However, the Full Moon turned up late, so it was all the non-combat characters. And the Lunar party actually took heavy casualties; one was knocked out, one lost an arm, one was killed. Most of the PCs actually fled, but then the Full Moon just chopped up all the enemy.<br /> <br /> Later, the Full Moon fought Katsunaga (the Earth aspect) by himself. It was a fight between two tough, strong, slow guys. The Full Moon got knocked prone right at the beginning, but then got up, soaked attacks, and disarmed the Earth Aspect. Unsurprisingly, a melee-ist doesn't do well with no weapon, and he got his head crushed.<br /> <br /> Then all of them except the two shamans came to kill the Full Moon (the other PCs were elsewhere). He ballsed up his first attack roll, and, well, then he was being attacked by a battle group and a bunch of DBs, and Overwhelming penalties tell, not to mention other penalties from Shining Ice Mirror, charms, etc. Even with a massive soak (19), they crashed him, and threw on a ton of damage (I think 18 lethal? Something like that). He lost an eye, but then there was an earthquake and so he fell off a cliff and into the water. Then he spent a week hibernating in walrus-form in a cave to heal all the damage.<br /> He did manage to kill 30 or 40 soldiers in the fight, but that's not all that significant compared to the Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> So then the Full Moon hid in some woods, and waited until the Water Aspect officer was on patrol. He snuck up behind her, ambushed her with an axe strike that took her to -4, and it was pretty inevitable after that. Then he looted her artefacts (jade medium armour and Rainwalker), but they don't work for him. He might give them to other PCs later though.<br /> <br /> So it's been... 6 sessions, I think, since they first fought some of these guys? Maybe 7. So they've certainly last me a while, they've basically been the main antagonists of the first and second story arcs. This session will be Session 10 of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Legion has lost about half its troops, and 4 Dragonblood. They have left:<br /> Kazei Jadis. <b>Air, \u201c</b>the white witch\u201d. Great at strategic manouevres, and good vs battle groups with her combat sorcery.<br /> Shozei Umi, <b>Air</b>. Uses Shining Ice Mirror. Took the Full Moon's eye.<br /> Shozei \u2013 Hatsuno, <b>Air</b>, \u201cFlashing Spear Lioness\u201d. Most optimised combat character.<br /> Deputy is Tazei Saizo, blind <b>Earth</b> swordsman. Good at command rolls, can also boost the infantry's soak+defence.<br /> Tazei Yukihiro, <b>Fire</b>. High Evasion and attack pools, that's pretty much it.<br /> Shugenja Goji, <b>Fire. </b>Not really a combat character, but not awful.<br /> Shugenja Itsuko, <b>Water</b>. Not really a combat character, but not awful.<br /> A size 4 unit of medium infantry, but they've had to replace some of their soldiers with local mercenaries, so it's Drill is only Average now, and not all their troops have medium armour.<br /> <br /> <br /> The PCs have lost a Changing Moon, the Walrus-totem Full Moon's eye, and the Gorilla-totem Casteless's arm. Their other Changing Moon has also been missing for about a month (she's not dead, just missing). But they've picked up a second Full Moon, who won them 100 Ice-Giants in a tug-of-war. So they've got left:<br /> Olaf Keelbreaker, <b>Full Moon</b>. Walrus-totem, one-eyed, one-tusked, wields a Moonsilver Grand Grimcleaver. Amazing at combat (for an E1 character, anyway).<br /> Krove, the Tiger-Bull, <b>Full Moon.</b> Strongest in the land. Has decent but not amazing combat pools and a few combat charms.<br /> Underfoot, lord of the Apes, <b>Casteless</b>. Has decent but not amazing combat pools and a few combat charms. Lost his arm, now it's replaced with a cursed snake arm which may bite both his enemies and him in combat.<br /> Mujin the merchant, <b>Casteless</b>. Has decent but not amazing combat pools and a Dexterity excellency.<br /> Atal the shaman, <b>No Moon</b>. The only one with good War pools (Int+War of 8), so I'm expecting him to stand at the back and give orders to the Ice-Giants.<br /> A size 3 unit of Ice-Giants (decent pools, lots of health levels).<br /> <br /> <br /> On Sunday's session we'll probably have some strategic manouevring, followed by a big battle between the two sides. I expect that to be pretty brutal, but my money is on the PCs. The enormous magnitude of Ice-Giants is a great tar pit. But I wouldn't be shocked by more injuries. I should think as well that it'll be pretty final; if a couple of DBs escape, they're going to know they can't take on the Lunars.<br /> <br /> It's possible though that the Lunars may not co-ordinate well, as some are in different places. The Full Moon, Olaf, is in the woods, Mujin is in the Dragonblood camp spying on them (as the water-shaman's toyboy), and the other three are with the Ice-Giants.<br /> Of course, it's also possible that Olaf will join the other three, Mujin will slip out and give them info, and then go back and wait for the perfect opportunity to stab a Dragonblood in the back or something.<br /> Or they may not fight for some reason; the 3 with the Ice-Giants are on their way to overthrow the King, not knowing that the Dragonblood already overthrew him. Maybe they'll parley and go home. But I think that very unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-23-2019, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24